IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VI, "Administrative Review": ss 111 to 115, and ss 116 to 123
-- (repealed). Piece ei4. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- How the rules are shaped (the same in every ei4 module):
--   * No DEONTIC rule. A duty is a BOOLEAN "applies" rule and, where the text sets a time, a DATE rule for the last day.
--   * A power or permission is a BOOLEAN. FALSE means "this section does not give it", not "it is forbidden".
--   * A judgment the text hands to the Commission is a BOOLEAN input named for that satisfaction; it is never worked out.
--   * A fact decided outside this piece's range is a plain input marked "out of range".
--   * "Within n days after d" ends on d plus n and that day counts (the keel's fork F4: the Interpretation Act is not deposited).
-- Hohfeld, for this Part: the Commission's power to rescind or amend (s 111) is the liability of the person the decision is about;
-- the person's power to ask for reconsideration (s 112(1)) is the Commission's liability to be asked, and its duty to reconsider
-- (s 112(2)) is the person's claim; the person's right to payment pending appeal (s 114(1)) is the Commission's duty to pay.

§ `Part VI -- Administrative Review`

§§ `s 111 Rescission or amendment of decision`

-- src:1808 | 111 The Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in any particular claim for benefits if new facts are presented or if it is satisfied that the decision was given without knowledge of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 111 (src:1808)
GIVEN `new facts are presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was given without knowledge of some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was based on a mistake as to some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` IF
       `new facts are presented`
    OR `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was given without knowledge of some material fact`
    OR `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was based on a mistake as to some material fact`

§§ `s 112 Reconsideration -- Commission`

-- The facts of one request for reconsideration. "Prescribed" is the Regulations' word: reg 78 (piece er5) says a request must be
-- in writing, with the information it lists, filed as the Commission's website directs; the rule takes the outcome as one BOOLEAN.
-- src:1810 | 112 (1) A claimant or other person who is the subject of a decision of the Commission, or the employer of the claimant, may make a request to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision at any time within
-- src:1811 | (a) 30 days after the day on which a decision is communicated to them; or
-- src:1812 | (b) any further time that the Commission may allow.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1) (src:1810-1812)
DECLARE `ei4 Request for reconsideration` HAS
    `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 78 (piece er5)
    `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS A DATE
    `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
    `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS A MAYBE DATE   -- NOTHING when it has allowed none (s 112(1)(b))

-- src:1810 | 112 (1) A claimant or other person who is the subject of a decision of the Commission, or the employer of the claimant, may make a request to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision at any time within
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1) (src:1810)
GIVEN request IS A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112(1) the requester is one of the persons who may request a reconsideration` IF
       request's `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision`
    OR request's `the requester is the employer of the claimant`

-- src:1811 | (a) 30 days after the day on which a decision is communicated to them; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1)(a) (src:1811)
GIVEN `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 112(1)(a) the last day to request a reconsideration within 30 days` IS
    `the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester`

-- src:1811 | (a) 30 days after the day on which a decision is communicated to them; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1)(a) (src:1811)
GIVEN request IS A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112(1)(a) the request is made within 30 days after the decision is communicated` IF
    request's `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST
        `s 112(1)(a) the last day to request a reconsideration within 30 days` (request's `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester`)

-- Assumed, not ruled: "any further time that the Commission may allow" is the Commission's judgment, so it arrives as the last day of the
-- time it has allowed; with none allowed the paragraph gives nothing (fork F-ei4-2).
-- src:1812 | (b) any further time that the Commission may allow.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1)(b) (src:1812)
GIVEN request IS A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112(1)(b) the request is made within any further time the Commission has allowed` IS
    CONSIDER request's `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN request's `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST lastday

-- src:1818 | 112.1 A decision of the Commission made under the Employment Insurance Regulations respecting the writing off of any penalty owing, amount payable or interest accrued on any penalty owing or amount payable is not subject to review under section 112.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112.1 (src:1818)
GIVEN `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision respects the writing off of a penalty owing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision respects the writing off of an amount payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision respects the writing off of interest accrued on a penalty owing or an amount payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` IF
        `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations`
    AND (   `the decision respects the writing off of a penalty owing`
         OR `the decision respects the writing off of an amount payable`
         OR `the decision respects the writing off of interest accrued on a penalty owing or an amount payable`)

-- The person's power: a request is "made under subsection (1)" when the requester is one of the persons named, the form and
-- manner are the prescribed ones, the time allowed has not run out, and the decision is not one that s 112.1 shields from review.
-- src:1810 | 112 (1) A claimant or other person who is the subject of a decision of the Commission, or the employer of the claimant, may make a request to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision at any time within
-- src:1811 | (a) 30 days after the day on which a decision is communicated to them; or
-- src:1812 | (b) any further time that the Commission may allow.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(1), s 112.1 (src:1810-1812) (src:1818)
GIVEN request IS A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
      `the decision is not subject to review under section 112` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` IF
        `s 112(1) the requester is one of the persons who may request a reconsideration` request
    AND request's `the request is in the prescribed form and manner`
    AND (   `s 112(1)(a) the request is made within 30 days after the decision is communicated` request
         OR `s 112(1)(b) the request is made within any further time the Commission has allowed` request)
    AND NOT (`the decision is not subject to review under section 112`)

-- The person's claim: the Commission "must reconsider its decision if a request is made under subsection (1)".
-- src:1814 | (2) The Commission must reconsider its decision if a request is made under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 112(2) (src:1814)
GIVEN request IS A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
      `the decision is not subject to review under section 112` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` IF
    `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` request `the decision is not subject to review under section 112`

§§ `s 113 Appeal to Employment Insurance Board of Appeal`

-- The text sets no time for the appeal: that is in the Department of Employment and Social Development Act (not deposited),
-- so no deadline is computed here (fork F-ei4-3). The "including" clause is read as adding decisions on further time to the
-- decisions made under s 112 (fork F-ei4-4), so either fact is enough.
-- src:1820 | 113 A party who is dissatisfied with a decision of the Commission made under section 112, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request, may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 113 (src:1820)
GIVEN `is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision of the Commission was made under section 112` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision of the Commission is in relation to further time to make a request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IF
        `is a party`
    AND `is dissatisfied with the decision`
    AND (   `the decision of the Commission was made under section 112`
         OR `the decision of the Commission is in relation to further time to make a request`)

§§ `s 114 Payment of benefit pending appeal`

-- Subsection (2)(a): the Commission's own appeal, brought within 21 days of the decision on the ground that the claimant ought to be
-- disentitled under section 36 (s 36 is outside this range: piece ei1 or ei2 carries it; the ground is a plain fact here).
-- src:1825 | (a) if the appeal to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal was brought within 21 days after the day on which the decision of the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, was given and on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 114(2)(a) (src:1825)
GIVEN `the day on which the decision was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` IS A DATE
      `the appeal was brought on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 36 (piece ei2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 114(2)(a) the appeal to the Appeal Division stops subsection (1) applying` IF
        `the day on which the appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` AT MOST
            (`the last day of` 21 `days after` `the day on which the decision was given`)
    AND `the appeal was brought on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36`

-- Subsection (2)(b): "any other case that the Commission may, with the approval of the Governor in Council, prescribe by regulation".
-- Regs 80 to 82 (piece er5) prescribe cases; whether a given case is one of them is an input here.
-- src:1824 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply
-- src:1825 | (a) if the appeal to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal was brought within 21 days after the day on which the decision of the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, was given and on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36; and
-- src:1826 | (b) in any other case that the Commission may, with the approval of the Governor in Council, prescribe by regulation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 114(2) (src:1824-1826)
GIVEN `the day on which the decision was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` IS A DATE
      `the appeal was brought on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one that the Commission has prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: regs 80 to 82 (piece er5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` IF
        `s 114(2)(a) the appeal to the Appeal Division stops subsection (1) applying`
            `the day on which the decision was given` `the day on which the appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` `the appeal was brought on the ground that the claimant ought to be disentitled under section 36`
    OR `the case is one that the Commission has prescribed by regulation`

-- The claimant's claim to be paid although an appeal is pending. A pending appeal is not a condition ("even though an appeal is pending").
-- src:1822 | 114 (1) If a claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of that Act, benefits are payable in accordance with the decision of the Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, even though an appeal is pending, and any benefits paid under this section after the decision of the Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, are to be treated as having been duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant, even if the final determination of the question is adverse to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 114(1) (src:1822)
GIVEN `the claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim for benefits is allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` IF
        (   `the claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
         OR `the claim for benefits is allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal`)
    AND NOT (`subsection (1) does not apply under subsection (2)`)

-- The claimant's protection from recovery. FALSE means s 114(1) gives no protection; it does not say the benefits are recoverable.
-- src:1822 | 114 (1) If a claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of that Act, benefits are payable in accordance with the decision of the Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, even though an appeal is pending, and any benefits paid under this section after the decision of the Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal, as the case may be, are to be treated as having been duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant, even if the final determination of the question is adverse to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 114(1) (src:1822)
GIVEN `the claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim for benefits is allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits were paid under this section after the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 114(1) benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant` IF
        `the benefits were paid under this section after the decision`
    AND `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending`
            `the claim for benefits is allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
            `the claim for benefits is allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal`
            `subsection (1) does not apply under subsection (2)`

